# warnings

## UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import defer` is currently lowered to a normal import, because an import in `b.js` comes after a deferred import of a module that has a top-level `await` or imports one. This changes execution timing because side effects run immediately instead of when the deferred import is first used. `experimental.importDefer` does not keep the deferred evaluation in this build yet.
   ╭─[ b.js:1:1 ]
   │
 1 │ import defer * as wait from './wait.js';
   │ ────────────────────┬───────────────────  
   │                     ╰───────────────────── The deferred phase is removed here.
───╯

```

